No.  I was looking for an altar you can sacrifice at while you are still 
a relatively weak character.  Since you probably want to donate later, 
this is not guaranteed with the mine town altar.  With two guaranteed 
altars not too deep in the dungeon (one of which is in mine town and the 
other is the one I would create in addition), you can both sacrifice and 
donate, at the possible cost of killing one priest.

> Sure it carries a priest, but that can be as much 
> of a benifit as it is a challenge, and having both an unattended altar 
> and an attended one would seem to accomplish nothing more then reduce the 
> amount of variability present in one game of nethack, and make the 
> 'luck' of finding an altar in the early dungeon less useful.

I would not care about making luck "less useful".  I think that you 
should not depend on luck in nethack but on skills.  Since the rng is 
inevitable, you cannot eliminate good or bad luck.  But you can provide 
means for skillful players to circumvent bad luck.  In general, this 
increases variety rather than diminishing it, because it adds to the 
ways of achieving a particular goal.  Therefore, I would prefer the 
solution of making it possible to create an altar by a (possibly costly) 
ritual to the one of just putting an additional guaranteed altar.  But I 
would prefer the latter to no change at all (even though this would 
indeed reduce variety slightly, whereas my preferred solution would 
increase it).

